<p>Questions:</p>
<ol type="1">
<li><p>Clarification on why we do expectation of losses.</p></li>
<li><p>How is a strategy, the same thing as an estimator? We want an estimator to estimate the true state of nature, however what <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?s(X)"> or <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Chat%7B%5Ctheta%7D"> does is produce an action right?</p></li>
<li><p>Intuition of minimax in the disease, physician setting as compared to a game. Also explain slide 18.</p></li>
<li><p>When do we consider lower quantant and diagonal lower quantant?</p></li>
<li><p>Can we say that all minimax are Bayes?</p></li>
<li><p>Are all Bayes strategies admissible?</p></li>
</ol>
<section id="kinds-of-knowledge-we-can-obtain-from-a-problem-with-statistical-uncertainty" class="level1">
<h1>1. Kinds of Knowledge we can obtain from a problem with statistical uncertainty</h1>
<section id="basic-elements-of-a-statistical-problem" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="basic-elements-of-a-statistical-problem">Basic elements of a Statistical Problem</h3>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?a%20%5Chspace%7B0.3%20em%7D%20%5Cepsilon%20%5Chspace%7B0.3%20em%7D%20A"> where a is a single <strong>action</strong> belonging to the <strong>action space.</strong></p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Ctheta%20%5Chspace%7B0.3%20em%7D%20%5Cepsilon%20%5Chspace%7B0.3%20em%7D%20%5CTheta"> where <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Ctheta"> is a single parameter or state of nature that belongs to a parameter space.</p>
<p><img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?l(%5Ctheta,%20a)"> is a consequence of taking action a when state of nature is <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Ctheta"> . i.e.&nbsp;given <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Ctheta"> (although maybe unknown) , when player performs an action what is the loss or gain? if $l(\theta, a) &gt; 0 $ then it’s interpreted as <strong>loss</strong> occured to player. If <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%3C%200"> then <strong>gain.</strong></p>
</section>
<section id="example" class="level3">
<h3 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="example">Example</h3>
<p>Suppose a physician(the player) sees a patient who may ( <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Ctheta%20=%20%5Ctheta_%7B1%7D">) or may not (<img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Ctheta%20=%20%5Ctheta_%7B2%7D">) truly have a disease. The true state is unknown; based on the symptoms or some diagnostic test (estimator of the parameter), the physician should decide whether or not she should treat him. While doing so, careful consideration must be taken because the estimator may not be accurate which leads to losses. Say test here is indicated by $X$ . <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?X%20=%20x_%7B1%7D"> if test suggests presence of disease, <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?x_%7B2%7D"> otherwise.</p>
<ul>
<li>For e.g.&nbsp;, if the true state of <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?%5Ctheta%20=%20%5Ctheta_%7B1%7D">, but your test result comes out <img src="https://latex.codecogs.com/png.latex?x_%7B2%7D">, then that may worsen symptoms in a patient - incurring loss in a sense.</li>
</ul>
